# My Contribution – Lab 2.3: TOTP MFA Implementation

I worked on implementing Time-Based One-Time Password (TOTP) authentication using Python and the PyOTP library.

### Tasks Completed
- Created a TOTP secret key using Python.
- Generated a QR code and configured it with the SafeAuth authenticator app.
- Verified that the OTP generated by Python matched the OTP in the authenticator app.
- Tested successful authentication using a valid OTP.
- Tested failed authentication using an incorrect OTP.
- Checked OTP rotation after 30 seconds and confirmed that a new OTP was generated.
- Prepared findings about possible TOTP authentication failures and their root causes.

### Root Causes of TOTP Failure
- Client and server clocks are not synchronized.
- Incorrect shared secret is configured.
- OTP expires after its 30-second validity period.
- Wrong account or QR code is scanned.
- Automatic time settings are disabled on the device.

### Conclusion
I successfully implemented and tested TOTP-based MFA. This lab helped me understand how OTP generation, verification, time synchronization, and authenticator apps work together to provide an additional layer of security.
